{{ label('f03.unadjusted') }}

## Adjusted disparities

A logistic regression of the denial on indicators for each group and the controls the public file allows: the logarithm of income with a flag where income is missing, the logarithm of the loan amount, loan to value in bands, debt to income in HMDA's bands, loan type, loan purpose, the automated underwriting system used, the year, and a fixed effect for each of the {{ v('f03.lenders_with_fixed_effect') }} lenders with enough applications of both outcomes to estimate one ({{ v('f03.fixed_effect_share') }} of applications), the rest sharing one. The fixed effect means a group is compared with the reference group at the same lender. Missing values are encoded as their own level, never dropped, because dropping them would drop a different share of each group.

